{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/23543-what-s-on-your-game-table","id":23543,"title":"What's on your game table?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-04T22:21:05-08:00","id":23543,"title":"What's on your game table?","content":"So... Let's say you're an ST or a DM/GM/All knowing dice god and you're gearing up for a Table Top session with yer gaming buddies. What's on your table? Books, dice and paper? Or do you have an entire toybox of maps, props, minis, stereo of atmospheric music and a buffet of soda and snacks? Are you the planning type setting up foe stats and NPC character notes way ahead of time or are you the fly by the cuff type with just a few notes to keep in the story on track and make the rest up as you go? Though this isn't a question so much about style as what tools do you use in your styles.<br /> <br /> Shall I go first? I fall somewhere in the middle of the extremes. I try and prepare a few things in advance like baddies and NPCs, but I know players can be very unpredictable and might wind up doing something that tosses all those characters out the window entirely. I have notes for storyline marking posts, but I leave how (and how quickly) the characters get to those points up to the players.<br /> <br /> I have not run a TT game in well over 10 years, but I hope to do so again soon so I have collected a box of items that I recall being useful. I may not need them, but I like having them around. So, for my players I have small folders for char sheets and enough note pads for about 5 people. A pencil box with pens, pencils and a ruler. I printed out an archive of every char sheet in every system I own books for. (That way if we need extra or someone's friend wants to join in I can just photocopy it cheap instead of having to hunt on a laptop and find a printer.)<br /> <br /> I have more D10's than GOD and need to get a bigger case to fit them in, but I can pull out a pouch or 5 if no one brought their own dice. I have soft toys since I know from experience regardless of groups and members something always gets tossed around or at someone in the heat of the game. So in my game box I have several Koosh balls and the ST gets a plush Holy Hand Grenade. It also gives figety players something to do besides pick at book bindings or start tearing up bits of paper.<br /> <br /> I have an ST gavel, cuz sometimes you just have to make rulings loud and final. And as a joke one group I was in allowed the use of a magic 8 ball if someone was especially argumentative or whiney they can leave a ruling up to chance. This was amusing as the 8 ball always seemed to favor the ST's decision. (Any more arguing got the Gavel)<br /> <br /> I have a heavier plastic binder and clipboard for the ST screen and all my notes and NPC sheets. From my D&amp;D days I have a vinyl roll out map with squares on one side and hexes on the other with special markers. I doubt I'll need this, but it might come in handy.<br /> <br /> I still need to get a bin to keep everything in, preferably with wheels so I can toss books in and transport it if we're going to play someplace other than my house. That's on my wish list.<br /> <br /> Know what else I don't have that is essential to a Table Top RPG? A TABLE! Yup. We don't have a dinning table anymore since house mates moved out about a year ago and took theirs with them. That's something I need to replace before I can start getting a new group together.<br /> <br /> Something that was brought up in another thread was food at people's games and there were a few really yummy sounding ideas that involved crock pots. So now I'll have to get myself one of those some time. Anyone else got a cool gaming set up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","user":"Darling_Rose","date":".  Posted by phone originally. Broke up wall-o-text 12-06-2013, 06:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T03:50:27-08:00","id":23657,"title":"","content":"I tend to plan sessions quite loosely, having just a few pages of notes and a few floeshed out NPCs made in advance. I rarely have any trouble making up things I need on the fly, and in my experience, the sessions get better that way - no railroading, no frustration over planned stuff which never materialises. Besides these notes, I usually have the core rulebooks close at hand, along with pencils, dice and something to drink. I never use music, and tend not to use miniatures or other props, though I sometimes create written handouts, and often prepare maps then and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T04:07:24-08:00","id":23665,"title":"","content":"-Core book and Camarilla Guide, not for me, for the players<br /> -Dices, character sheets, pencils and erasers<br /> -Notebook for images, portraits, the occasional video and background musics (played strictly on Winamp)<br /> -Maps ripped from somewhere, printed and scribbled<br /> -Chips, popcorn, 1-2 soft drink and 1-2 beers<br /> -Jabba the Cat (a big Norwegian Forest Cat usually jumping on table and players)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 12-05-2013, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T06:41:47-08:00","id":23721,"title":"","content":"I seem to GM pretty light compared to other folks. I've got my dice, relevant game books the players might need for reference, and my ipad with my game notes.<br /> <br /> They players are usually the ones that supply the beer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T14:49:35-08:00","id":23990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I've gotta add... I'd be leery of anyone handing me a koosh ball for my RP session. Especially if they told me it was for &quot;fidgety players.&quot; It's either extraordinarily condescending to the player or a frightening indication of a storyteller that is going to be incapable of keeping the table engaged.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think maybe I must be playing with people with some mild form of Aspergers. In fact while I was trying to look up info on Koosh toys I found they're a favorite fidget toy of many people with Aspergers. It would explain why some of my friends are either tearing up bits of paper or clicking their pens or mechanical pencils to the point of driving everyone else at the table crazy. As I did a bit more research into these habits I found I had a few myself. Mainly pen chewing and nail biting. It's not because Im bored with the game or can't focus. I just need something to do with my hands when it's not my turn. I wouldn't call it condescending or a poor judgment on the ST if other people have the same need. A koosh is a lot quieter than a ball point pen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T15:49:36-08:00","id":24033,"title":"","content":"I ST much like Loxosceles, evidently.<br /> <br /> At my table, I have:<br /> Tablet computer. It has music, internet (for quickly pulling up a random picture of whatever NPC my players are trying to screw over), notes, digital copies of the books, so much stuff. Seriously, they're so useful - I've almost completely eliminated paper on and around my table.<br /> ST Screen. I use one that has space for homemade inserts, plus it's in a landscape style, rather than portrait, so I can watch my players better.<br /> Dice. Including my super-special &quot;Storyteller dice,&quot; which have no 1's, but two 10's. Before the flaming torches and pitchforks come out, I use them only for NPC rolls, and NPC's don't get to specialize and do not benefit from &quot;exploding 10's,&quot; or rerolling, or whatever system you may use, but the narrative demands that they don't trip and fall down an elevator shaft or accidentally shoot themselves in the face, either.<br /> Dice tray. <b>Everyone needs one of these, </b>they are so nice. I've built a couple after being asked to by players, and they love them.<br /> I have several mechanical pencils around the house that players are welcome to use, but I ask them to bring their own. Players are also welcome to bring any books they like, but I've found - with my group, at least - eliminating the stack of books around the table discourages distraction. Instead, I encourage them to write down anything about their powers that they need to know - Mr. Gone's add-on sheets are excellent tools, for both me and the players. We use either my dining room or coffee table, depending on myriad factors, mostly whether or not my girlfriend is gong to bed early. We put down the vinyl hex-mat which doubles as a tablecloth and impromptu notepad, forever solving the coasters debate.<br /> <br /> As for the Koosh ball thing, it all depends on situation and presentation. In a group of friends, I don't think it would be seen as condescending. We had a player that loved rolling dice, always, forever, for no reason other than fidgeting. Rolling them on the table, rolling them around in his hand, flicking them like marbles into the dice tray - even when it was his turn and he was engaged with the story, he'd still be playing with the dice. Then another player gave him one of those Stkfas toys, and now he only touches the dice when he needs to. Now that's completely different then if you're meeting at say, a college gaming club, and the first thing that happens is the ST handing out Koosh balls and saying &quot;If you need to fidget during the game, play with this.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T03:45:16-08:00","id":24268,"title":"","content":"Sounds like lots of people use a tablet. All my books are on a bookshelf (along with the booze) right next to where I hope to put the table. I've never considered using a tablet device for pulling up PDFs. Course I've also never owned a tablet. I suppose I should look into investing in one cheap one to give me a resource for pulling up quick images and looking up any books that I don't have on the shelf (though admittedly there's only a few missing from the systems I would be able to ST.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/23543-what-s-on-your-game-table?p=24033#post24033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Koosh ball thing, it all depends on situation and presentation. In a group of friends, I don't think it would be seen as condescending. We had a player that loved rolling dice, always, forever, for no reason other than fidgeting. Rolling them on the table, rolling them around in his hand, flicking them like marbles into the dice tray - even when it was his turn and he was engaged with the story, he'd still be playing with the dice. Then another player gave him one of those Stkfas toys, and now he only touches the dice when he needs to. Now that's completely different then if you're meeting at say, a college gaming club, and the first thing that happens is the ST handing out Koosh balls and saying &quot;If you need to fidget during the game, play with this.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah no, I wouldn't be tossing them out like that. I'd just leave em on the table and let whoever wants to play with them play with them.<br /> <br /> I'm a little iffy on the dice tray. Is this mainly for an even surface or are your players just that enthusiastic with the dice rolling? I've seen dice towers, but those seem to just take up a lot of space and are just there to keep the other players from calling &quot;CHEATER!&quot; when someone doesn't send the dice rolling very far and winds up with a high number. How big are these dice trays? I also find Nothing's point of NPCs having Botch proof dice. Normally I roll for NPCs behind the screen. If there's a botch I just re-roll.<br /> <br /> Side Note, I LOVE Mr. Gone's add on sheets. They are indeed very useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","user":"Darling_Rose","date":".  typos 12-06-2013, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T10:39:39-08:00","id":24441,"title":"","content":"I bring my books, my ST Screen for when I have to hide dice rolls, and a notebook. If I'm hosting, I stock the fridge. If someone else is hosting, I let them know before they agree to host that they're on refreshments duty, which means at least one 6-pack of Mountain Dew reserved for myself.<br /> <br /> I haven't run a game since laptops became so cheap or tablets came out, so I'd probably have less to bring with me now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T17:09:53-08:00","id":24757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loxosceles</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thread of &quot;What's in your game room?&quot; would produce a different answer than one of what's at the table.</div> </div> </div> </div> Very true. I have an office/nerd cave where I store all my physical books (and toys &amp; the like), where players can't get their greasy hands on them.<br /> <br /> As to the dice tray, I think they're fanstatsic. I've built several myself, just from materials from the local arts &amp; crafts shop. They cut the clatter of dice rolling on a tabletop, but if you like that sound, you can use a base to replicate it without worrying about your table. Personally, I like (mostly) silent rolling, so I use a 6x4 inch tray with a thin layer of foam over cork board, mounted on balsa wood, with a felt flooring. I've built some for players that prefer more bounce - felt, foam, balsa wood, no cork - and one for a player that wanted more &quot;clatter&quot; but not as much as bare wood (simple - thin felt over the wood). In the center of the table I have a 9x11 oval, which my players love. No corners for dice to get stuck in, the lip is an inch high, so no rogue dice rolling under a chair or table, a dark grey felt for great contrast - I'm really proud of it. My only regret is I didn't paint the damn thing before I put it together, so now it's that neutral grain instead of something cool. As for cheating, well.. it's not <i>the</i> reason I use dice trays, but I did have a player that loved fudging his rolls, and this had put a stop to it. While no one ever said the dice tray was a check on him, he did seem resentful about it and treated it like a craps table.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-08T03:36:55-08:00","id":25723,"title":"","content":"Nothing:<br /> <br /> Those do indeed sound like awesome game trays. I wonder where I can find one. but I'll need one small enough I can fit it in a backpack or stick a supplement book inside it to save space. Any suggestions where to look will be most appreciated. I think I will start a new thread about game rooms next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}